      "description": "Watch Ipswich vs Sunderland highlights and goals from Premier League International Cup on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 22, 2026. Ipswich and Sunderland faced off in a high-stakes Premier League International Cup encounter on 2026-08-22 . The atmosphere at the stadium promised a night of intense tactical battle, where clinical finishing would eventually clash with dominant possession. A Balanced Opening Act The match ignited in the 24th minute when Ipswich took advantage of a defensive lapse. A blunder by Luke O'Nien allowed Julio Enciso to slide a pass to Emersonn , who made no mistake with a right-footed finish to break the deadlock. Despite the setback, Sunderland maintained their composure and continued to dictate the tempo of the game. Their persistence was rewarded in the 39th minute through a moment of individual brilliance. Nilson Angulo stepped up to a direct free kick and curled a magnificent strike into the back of the net. The equalizer sent both teams into the halftime break level, with the game hanging perfectly in the balance after a high-energy first half. Tension Rises in the Second Half The second period saw a rise in physicality as the referee reached for his pocket multiple times. Daniel Ballard , Nilson Angulo , and Luke O'Nien were all booked as the battle for midfield supremacy intensified. Ipswich nearly regained the lead in spectacular fashion when Julio Enciso attempted an audacious bicycle kick that whistled just wide of the target. As the clock ticked toward the final ten minutes, both managers turned to their benches, introducing fresh energy for the closing stages. Sunderland continued to dominate the ball with 62% possession, but the Ipswich defense, anchored by Dara O'Shea and Jacob Greaves , remained resolute under pressure. Late Drama at the Death Just as the match seemed destined for a draw, the definitive moment arrived in the 90th minute. A defensive error by Omar Alderete proved costly as Sasa Lukic pounced, setting up Jack Clarke for a dramatic right-footed winner. The stadium erupted as the hosts snatched the lead in the final moments of regulation time. Four minutes of stoppage time saw Sunderland throw everything forward. Kjell Scherpen produced vital interventions, intercepting dangerous crosses and organizing his backline to withstand the late onslaught. Despite a late chance for Clarke to double his tally, Ipswich held firm to secure a hard-fought victory in front of nearly 30,000 fans."
